WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.930
In Active Directory,
a Windows PC joined to

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.975
the domain gets two jobs
done almost for free.

3
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:07.325
Job one is the name.

4
00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:11.007
The PC has a computer name,
say pc-zero-zero-four-two,

5
00:00:11.007 --> 00:00:16.575
and a primary DNS suffix, which is usually
the name of the AD domain it joined.

6
00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:19.438
Put them together and
you get its full name,

7
00:00:19.438 --> 00:00:22.137
its FQDN, or fully qualified domain name.

8
00:00:22.137 --> 00:00:24.662
Job two is the DNS record.

9
00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:27.783
An A record maps a name
to an IPv4 address;

10
00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:33.833
an AAAA record maps a name to an IPv6
address; and a PTR record goes the other way,

11
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.425
address to name, in what's
called a reverse zone.

12
00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:42.313
Dynamic update is the standard way to add
or change those records over the network.

13
00:00:42.313 --> 00:00:47.631
In AD, the domain's DNS zone lives in
the directory, on domain controllers,

14
00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:51.687
and by default it accepts
only secure dynamic updates.

15
00:00:51.687 --> 00:00:57.225
Secure means the update is signed with
Kerberos, AD's ticket-based sign-in protocol,

16
00:00:57.225 --> 00:01:00.563
and once a name exists, only
its owner can change it.

17
00:01:00.563 --> 00:01:04.912
The domain-joined PC has a machine
account in AD, so it can sign.

18
00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:08.214
By default, the PC
registers its own A record

19
00:01:08.214 --> 00:01:11.699
and the Windows DHCP
server registers the PTR.

20
00:01:11.699 --> 00:01:16.675
When AD retires, both jobs need a new
owner, and the second one is harder.

21
00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:23.102
Sources: Book 08, Chapter 04, What
AD-integrated DNS actually is,

22
00:01:23.102 --> 00:01:29.780
and Secure dynamic updates and
the DHCP server; Microsoft Learn,

23
00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:37.030
Dynamic update (Windows Server DNS)
[S26]; Policy CSP ADMX_DnsClient [S27].
